   ```tsx
         {asking ? (
           // An inline question, not a modal, as a friend row's: a block lifted later restores no request (§9.4, #2684).
           <span className="together-row__actions" role="alertdialog" aria-labelledby={questionId}>
             <span className="together-row__question" id={questionId}>
               <Named text={t("Block {name}? Their request goes, and neither of you can reach the other.")} name={other.username} />
             </span>
             <button
               type="button"
               data-testid={togetherTestid.confirm}
               disabled={busy}
               onClick={() => {
                 setAsking(false);
                 onBlock?.();
               }}
             >
               {t("Block")}
             </button>
             <button
               type="button"
               className="link-button"
               data-testid={togetherTestid.keep}
               onClick={() => {
                 setAsking(false);
               }}
             >
               {t("Keep")}
             </button>
           </span>
         ) : (
           <span className="together-row__actions">
             …the existing incoming/outgoing children, unchanged except the Block button below…
           </span>
         )}
   ```
   In the existing children, change only the `requestBlock` button. Its `onClick={onBlock}` becomes:
   ```tsx
   onClick={() => {
     setAsking(true);
   }}
   ```
   Keep that button's `type`, `className`, `data-testid` and `disabled={busy}` exactly as they are. Leave the Accept, Decline and Cancel buttons and the outgoing branch unchanged. Do not edit the comment `/** One request, either way (B55). */` or the file header (lines 1-8).

